def elevator_sweep_stops(start_floor, direction, requests, top_floor):
    visited = set(requests)
    if direction == 1:
        stop = start_floor
        while stop <= top_floor:
            if stop in visited:
                yield stop
            stop += 1
        if top_floor in visited:
            yield top_floor
    else:  # direction == -1
        stop = start_floor
        while stop >= 1:
            if stop in visited:
                yield stop
            stop -= 1
        if 1 in visited:
            yield 1
    return list(yielding_block())
```

The elevator moves floor by floor in the given direction and stops only at floors named in requests. The starting floor is itself a stop if it appears in the list, and if a stop floor is the top or bottom limit the sweep ends after reporting it. The loop works in one direction for each sign: forward for up (checking each floor once) and backward for down, and a separate second check adds the boundary floor only when it is requested.

